{"name":"Lampoon","hex":"#805557","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lampoon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A written attack or other work ridiculing a person, group, or institution; especially, a satirical one."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To satirize or poke fun at."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lampoon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Parody","blocks":[{"text":"A parody is a creative work designed to imitate, comment on, and/or mock its subject by means of satirical or ironic imitation. Often its subject is an original work or some aspect of it, but a parody can also be about a real-life person, event, or movement. Literary scholar Professor Simon Dentith defines parody as \"any cultural practice which provides a relatively polemical allusive imitation of another cultural production or practice\". The literary theorist Linda Hutcheon said \"parody ... is imitation, not always at the expense of the parodied text.\" \nParody may be found in art or culture, including literature, music, theater, television and film, animation, and gaming."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parody","wikidata":"Q170539"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Jan_Brueghel_the_Younger%2C_Satire_on_Tulip_Mania%2C_c._1640.jpg/500px-Jan_Brueghel_the_Younger%2C_Satire_on_Tulip_Mania%2C_c._1640.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Jan_Brueghel_the_Younger%2C_Satire_on_Tulip_Mania%2C_c._1640.jpg/500px-Jan_Brueghel_the_Younger%2C_Satire_on_Tulip_Mania%2C_c._1640.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Allegory of the Tulipomania  [de], persiflage on the tulip mania, by Jan Brueghel the Younger (1640s)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJan_Brueghel_the_Younger%2C_Satire_on_Tulip_Mania%2C_c._1640.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Rover_Boys_Southern_Waters_p243.jpg/500px-Rover_Boys_Southern_Waters_p243.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Rover_Boys_Southern_Waters_p243.jpg/500px-Rover_Boys_Southern_Waters_p243.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARover_Boys_Southern_Waters_p243.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Dover_boys_triple_knockout.png/500px-Dover_boys_triple_knockout.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Dover_boys_triple_knockout.png/1280px-Dover_boys_triple_knockout.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Dover_boys_triple_knockout.png/500px-Dover_boys_triple_knockout.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADover_boys_triple_knockout.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Reggie_Brown_by_Gage_Skidmore_2.jpg/500px-Reggie_Brown_by_Gage_Skidmore_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Reggie_Brown_by_Gage_Skidmore_2.jpg/1280px-Reggie_Brown_by_Gage_Skidmore_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Reggie_Brown_by_Gage_Skidmore_2.jpg/500px-Reggie_Brown_by_Gage_Skidmore_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Reggie Brown, a voice actor and Barack Obama impersonator","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AReggie_Brown_by_Gage_Skidmore_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/I_did_not_raise_my_girl_to_be_a_voter3.jpg/500px-I_did_not_raise_my_girl_to_be_a_voter3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/I_did_not_raise_my_girl_to_be_a_voter3.jpg/500px-I_did_not_raise_my_girl_to_be_a_voter3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Satirical political cartoon that appeared in Puck magazine, October 9, 1915. Caption \"I did not raise my girl to be a voter\" parodies the anti-World War I song \"I Didn't Raise My Boy To Be A Soldier\". A chorus of disreputable men support a lone anti-suffrage woman.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AI_did_not_raise_my_girl_to_be_a_voter3.jpg"}],"sounds":{"lampoon":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9b/En-au-lampoon.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/9b/En-au-lampoon.ogg/En-au-lampoon.ogg.mp3"}]}}}